  "notes": "A multi-instrumentalist hip-hop-soul producer bridging Kanye-orbit rap and 2000s R&B; the research windows him 2005–2010 and gives \"96–110 straight\", mode 107, the sourced tempo. Three drum deltas from \"live-instrumentation-forward — a programmed kick/snare grid with played ride, hat and hand percussion over it\": `quantizeStrength` falls to 0.58 with `velocityVar` at 0.28 and the snare 4–10 ms off the grid, the hat moves to a played 8th base at 0.34 fill density, and the perc bed is a four-lane ride/conga/bongo/tambourine set at three to seven hits a bar. The entry also states a negative that is authored as one: \"moderate 16th hat density, **no trap-style rolls**\", so `rolls.freqPerBar` sits at 0.03 — near-zero for a model at this tempo, and a real delta from the parent's 0.3. Harmony comes from the biography: \"he came up playing in church and leading the Jazz Funk Project band\" and \"he plays **piano, drums, bass, guitar and organ**\", so the model authors 4-chord cycles with a 0.14 triad share and organ colour rather than a two-chord bed. The bass is the same claim: \"played electric bass or organ pedal rather than sustained 808; **the low end moves**\" — `followRootsProb` 0.52 with walking cells and no `bass808` block. \"A guitar or horn countermelody\" is the counter at +12 at a 0.5 density. ⚠ Confidence is medium: instrumentation and credits are sourced, the tempo band is catalogue-derived. ⚠ Every velocity and density number is INFERRED. ⚠ `session.keys` is INFERRED: the entry's Keys line gives \"minor-mode with jazz/gospel extensions — he came up playing in church and leading the Jazz Funk Project band\" and enumerates no tonic, so the values here and their weights are this author's reading of that line.",
